MID_SE_Die_Iio_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Die_Iio_C_001: Diego. Do you have a moment?
MID_SE_Die_Iio_C_002: What?
MID_SE_Die_Iio_C_003: I've noticed you're called Orchel's stray. You're\nquite devoted to her.
MID_SE_Die_Iio_C_004: But why? How does a skilled fighter like you become\nso...subordinate.
MID_SE_Die_Iio_C_005: Why should I tell you? Well, whatever. Orchel is\nlike...a merciful goddess.
MID_SE_Die_Iio_C_006: She takes in orphans and sometimes serves food to\nthe other priests.
MID_SE_Die_Iio_C_007: I see. She treats everyone as equals. And she's\nhonorable. Anything else?
MID_SE_Die_Iio_C_008: She believes the best of everyone. It gets her into\ntrouble with some merchants, so I have to watch her.
MID_SE_Die_Iio_C_009: Also she can be clumsy and unfocused. I've seen\nher so lost in thought that she bumps into a wall.
MID_SE_Die_Iio_C_010: Huh. And what do you get from serving such\na master?
MID_SE_Die_Iio_C_011: I don't know. Why?
MID_SE_Die_Iio_C_012: I've always strived to become the ideal knight. One\nwho protects the happiness of the people.
MID_SE_Die_Iio_C_013: I seek a lord who's worthy of my service and whose\nideals mirror my own. Someone who can lead!
MID_SE_Die_Iio_C_014: Hmm.
MID_SE_Die_Iio_C_015: Sorry. It's a topic I'm quite passionate about,\nbut I sense you're not.
MID_SE_Die_Iio_C_016: You don't sound too experienced, for a mercenary.
MID_SE_Die_Iio_C_017: I began as a knight for the kingdom of Arago.
MID_SE_Die_Iio_C_018: But King Gilchris and his knights were self-serving\nand only wanted power. It's why I left.
MID_SE_Die_Iio_C_019: Ah. So you abandoned your lord in favor of\nyour ideals.
MID_SE_Die_Iio_C_020: That's where I'm different. I don't need my lady to\nmirror my beliefs.
MID_SE_Die_Iio_C_021: So there are ideals you live by then?
MID_SE_Die_Iio_C_022: I'm done talking with you.
MID_SE_Die_Iio_C_023: OK, I'll let it go. Maybe I'll see what your ideals are\nout on the battlefield.
MID_SE_Die_Iio_C_024: *sigh* Just don't get in my way.
MID_SE_Die_Iio_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Die_Iio_B_001: What is it, Io? And how soon can we get it\nover with?
MID_SE_Die_Iio_B_002: I've been watching you for a while now, and I think\nI finally understand.
MID_SE_Die_Iio_B_003: You and I view loyalty differently. To you, it's all\nabout service and nothing more.
MID_SE_Die_Iio_B_004: That's all I need it to be.
MID_SE_Die_Iio_B_005: Maybe, but why do you serve? There must be some\nreason, or it wouldn't matter who your lord was.
MID_SE_Die_Iio_B_006: Tch. You're not going to let it go, are you.\nFine, then.
MID_SE_Die_Iio_B_007: Back in the Har Hali, I would do whatever the\nchief told me to.
MID_SE_Die_Iio_B_008: Until we were told to kill each other and offer our\nsouls. That was the day I ran away.
MID_SE_Die_Iio_B_009: I didn't even have the excuse of some high-minded\nideals backing up my choice.
MID_SE_Die_Iio_B_010: Mm...
MID_SE_Die_Iio_B_011: I went on the run, and Orchel saved my life. Now I\ncan't imagine serving anyone else.
MID_SE_Die_Iio_B_012: Supporting her is where I find my happiness.
MID_SE_Die_Iio_B_013: Then protecting her, serving her is your reason—your\nideal. And that's enough for you.
MID_SE_Die_Iio_B_014: Because I'm not a knight. Do you see? I don't have\nthe answers you're looking for.
MID_SE_Die_Iio_B_015: That's not true. It's become clear that you and Orchel\nhave a relationship beyond that of a lord and vassal.
MID_SE_Die_Iio_B_016: Frankly, I'm jealous. I still haven't found a lord to\nserve the way you have.
MID_SE_Die_Iio_B_017: Well, keep trying. I personally never held your style\nof noble ideals.
MID_SE_Die_Iio_B_018: But if you hold on to yours, sooner or later you'll\nfind someone you can be proud to serve.
MID_SE_Die_Iio_B_019: Thank you, Diego.
MID_SE_Die_Iio_B_020: Don't thank me. Just be careful.
MID_SE_Die_Iio_B_021: If the master you find is Orchel's enemy, then I'll\ncome at you both with everything I have.
MID_SE_Die_Iio_B_022: I'd definitely like to avoid that. You would make for\na dangerous foe.